` stays pending; `over_quota` stays pending and stops the run (`quota`); `retry_after_seconds` holds the next batch until `retryAt`. A refused request (a thrown `V1Error`) keeps its batch pending: 429 `RATE_LIMITED` and 503 `SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE` wait `retryAfterSeconds` (`waiting`, `retryAt`) and send the same batch again, for at most 2 minutes, then stop `paused`; 503 `AI_PAUSED` or `IMPORTS_PAUSED` stops `paused`; 403 `AI_CONSENT_REQUIRED` stops `consent`; 404 stops `unavailable`; a lost answer or no network stops `offline` (the next run sends the batch again and the server answers `duplicate`); a diary write refused after the session moved (`StaleEpochError`, `DiaryLocked`) stops the run with nothing more sent. `stop()` ends after the batch in flight. A run clears `lastStop` as it starts; a `user` or `quota` stop stores it with the Bangkok day. At the end one `trackSlipScanFinished` and `lastRunAt`. `secondsLeft` is pending times the run's own seconds per uploaded slip.
- `connect` stores albums and the start date (never more than 90 days back, C10), watermarks at that date, and sends `trackAlbumsConnected`; `disconnect` stops at once, releases the pending picked copies, keeps the known hashes (C7) and sends `trackAlbumsDisconnected`.
- **`SlipsProvider`** is mounted once, in P2-T18's `WalletShell` around `AddTrayHost`, so Home, the add tray and every slip route share one engine and store. Without props its deps are `appSlipDeps(accountId, store, locale)` from `useDiaryView().accountId` and `useSpendDiary()?.slipScanStore()` while a diary is ready (else null), and its engine is `slipEngineFor(accountId, deps)`.
- `sendOneSlip` (B19, A1, A32): no bank slip QR is `not_slip` and a shrink of null `too_large`, each with nothing sent; else one `live` batch of one with the given origin and `last: false` (the sheet shows the draft, so no push); a 429 is waited out once (its `retryAfterSeconds`, at most 10 s) and sent again; any other refusal throws `V1Error` with its status and code (403 `AI_CONSENT_REQUIRED`, 404 `NOT_FOUND`, 429 `RATE_LIMITED`, 503 `AI_PAUSED`, `IMPORTS_PAUSED` or `SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE`), as do network and session failures.

